cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Earth Pulse in your work, please cite this software repository."
title: "Earth Pulse"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Earth Pulse Contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/cyberhatc/earth-pulse"
url: "https://earth-pulse-kkud.vercel.app/"
abstract: >-
  Earth Pulse is an open-source environmental investigation platform for the
  NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026 (Be An Earth System Trend Detective). It
  combines Earth observation data workflows, robust statistical analysis,
  machine-learning forecasting and anomaly detection, geospatial exploration,
  and evidence-grounded explanations to help users investigate place-based
  environmental change with explicit provenance, uncertainty, and limitations.
keywords:
  - climate
  - earth-observation
  - nasa-space-apps
  - environmental-data
  - trend-analysis
  - forecasting
  - geospatial
  - open-source
  - fastapi
  - react
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-11-16
